1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
To be continued...

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
...demons, devils, and bloodsuckers.

3
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:33,840
Let's see, where to begin?

4
00:00:34,300 --> 00:00:36,600
Don't. You can spare us the lecture, Shinoa.

5
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:38,040
Let's do this.

6
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:39,060
Hold it.

7
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:41,880
You're gonna try it at the same time?

8
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:43,200
What if something goes wrong?

9
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:45,580
Your demon could get out of control.

10
00:00:46,140 --> 00:00:48,340
You remember when Yoichi tried to kill us?

11
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:51,440
That's why we came out here, so you can't hurt anything.

12
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:53,320
Out of control?

13
00:00:55,480 --> 00:00:56,880
Huh? What did you say?

14
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:57,760
Nothing.

15
00:00:58,720 --> 00:00:59,640
Hey, guys!

16
00:01:00,960 --> 00:01:01,820
What is it?

17
00:01:02,860 --> 00:01:04,620
It's the four horsemen of John.

18
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:08,500
Three of them.

19
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:10,380
No, make that five.

20
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:13,060
Crap. We need to deal with them.

21
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:15,260
All right. Let's get this over with fast.

22
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:18,900
Destroy our enemies, Gekkoine.

23
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:20,500
Let's protect everyone.

24
00:01:20,500 --> 00:01:40,440
You guys, I did it.

25
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:43,640
Did you just manifest your demons? Since when can you do that?

26
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,700
Explain how that's possible, Shinoa.

27
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:47,980
Have you been giving him private lessons or something?

28
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:50,680
No. Yoichi's mastered manifestation on his own.

29
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:53,020
He's always had exceptional curse control abilities.

30
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:56,140
He's got a surprisingly strong relationship with his demon.

31
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:57,340
Seriously?

32
00:01:57,340 --> 00:02:02,400
Yeah. I've been talking to my demon before I go to sleep and in my dreams.

33
00:02:02,560 --> 00:02:04,100
Now I just sort of get how to do it.

34
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:10,100
Okay, Ashuromaru. Drink my blood.

35
00:02:10,180 --> 00:02:10,860
You wait!

36
00:02:10,860 --> 00:02:18,960
Prepare to fight!

37
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:31,440
Is he okay?

38
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:33,160
What just happened to him?

39
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:34,280
I'm not sure.

40
00:02:34,660 --> 00:02:37,600
He didn't immediately go berserk, so that's a big improvement.

41
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:41,220
Right now, he's more than likely trying to make contact with his demon.

42
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:44,780
We'll have to stand watch over him until he regains full consciousness.

43
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:46,520
Don't look so worried.

44
00:02:46,640 --> 00:02:48,880
We're here to look out for our family, aren't we, boy?

45
00:04:19,009 --> 00:04:21,009
You

46
00:04:30,869 --> 00:04:34,689
Trouble as usual. What do you mean? It's not you's fault

47
00:04:36,969 --> 00:04:38,469
Just saying

48
00:04:38,469 --> 00:04:44,769
Yoichi and I were interrogated and tortured by the Hiragis the whole reason is because they wanted to know more about what he did

49
00:04:45,369 --> 00:04:47,769
Yeah, and what did you tell them about it?

50
00:04:47,769 --> 00:04:52,689
Exactly what you ordered us to but I didn't know what they were talking about

51
00:04:53,009 --> 00:04:58,769
You did the right thing and you still think it's smart that we don't tell you he completely lost control

52
00:04:59,969 --> 00:05:06,509
Because it kind of looks like you're trying to manipulate him for some reason, but you wouldn't do that to your teammate, right?

53
00:05:06,769 --> 00:05:12,169
What if I did I don't know? I'd still follow orders to keep my sister safe

54
00:05:12,709 --> 00:05:17,689
I'd have to swallow down vomit every time I saw you. Hey, you can't talk to your superior like that

55
00:05:17,769 --> 00:05:20,689
She know what is just trying to protect you from the people in the upper

56
00:05:20,689 --> 00:05:22,689
It's okay, Mitsu

57
00:05:22,689 --> 00:05:25,689
And what about you, Yoichi? What do you think?

58
00:05:25,689 --> 00:05:26,689
Oh

59
00:05:26,689 --> 00:05:28,689
well, I

60
00:05:28,689 --> 00:05:29,109
I

61
00:05:29,109 --> 00:05:35,209
Get why you don't want to tell you about what happened when he lost control because that might cause him to freak out, but

62
00:05:35,209 --> 00:05:38,129
You want a better explanation, don't you?

63
00:05:38,129 --> 00:05:39,129
Hmm

64
00:05:39,129 --> 00:05:43,329
We're comrades, aren't we? So tell us your reasoning

65
00:05:43,329 --> 00:05:49,669
You're right about that. We should trust each other. Keeping secrets could drive us apart

66
00:05:49,669 --> 00:05:51,329
All right, then

67
00:05:51,329 --> 00:05:55,809
Let's talk about all of this when you's awake and the training's over

68
00:05:55,809 --> 00:06:00,729
Not just about what happened to him, but about where we stand as a unit, too

69
00:06:00,729 --> 00:06:02,729
Can I get all your help here, you guys?

70
00:06:02,729 --> 00:06:03,729
Can I get all your help here, you guys?

71
00:06:03,729 --> 00:06:04,729
Can I get all your help here, you guys?

72
00:06:04,729 --> 00:06:05,729
Can I get all your help here, you guys?

73
00:06:05,729 --> 00:06:07,729
Can I get all your help here, you guys?

74
00:06:07,729 --> 00:06:08,729
Hold him!

75
00:06:08,729 --> 00:06:09,729
Looks like it's starting

76
00:06:09,729 --> 00:06:10,729
Looks like it's starting

77
00:06:10,729 --> 00:06:11,729
Yeah, I think he's finally found his doom

78
00:06:11,729 --> 00:06:13,729
He never should have been born

79
00:06:13,729 --> 00:06:15,729
We must kill the Seraph of the End

80
00:06:15,729 --> 00:06:31,729
He's the devil's child, not our son

81
00:06:31,729 --> 00:06:33,729
The boy is a monster

82
00:06:33,729 --> 00:06:36,729
Dad, what's wrong?

83
00:06:36,729 --> 00:06:38,729
You, don't fight it

84
00:06:38,729 --> 00:06:40,729
Come here

85
00:06:40,729 --> 00:06:44,729
I'm gonna send you to a better place, son

86
00:06:44,729 --> 00:07:04,729
You should have died here with the others

87
00:07:04,729 --> 00:07:08,729
Everyone else is dead because you ran away like a coward

88
00:07:08,729 --> 00:07:11,729
Fall apart, you

89
00:07:11,729 --> 00:07:16,729
If you think this memory will make me lose control, Ashura Maru

90
00:07:16,729 --> 00:07:18,729
Then you've underestimated me

91
00:07:18,729 --> 00:07:21,729
And how much there is at stake

92
00:07:21,729 --> 00:07:24,729
I made him a promise and I intend to keep it

93
00:07:24,729 --> 00:07:26,729
Come on, you

94
00:07:26,729 --> 00:07:28,729
Let's protect our family together

95
00:07:28,729 --> 00:07:30,729
Please, I'm counting on you

96
00:07:30,729 --> 00:07:31,729
I know

97
00:07:31,729 --> 00:07:34,729
I couldn't save you if you didn't want my help

98
00:07:34,729 --> 00:07:37,729
I won't fall for any of your demonic tricks

99
00:07:37,729 --> 00:07:51,729
Oh man, I thought I had you there for a second

100
00:07:51,729 --> 00:07:54,729
I know how you fight and this time I was prepared

101
00:07:54,729 --> 00:07:56,729
No need to act so tough

102
00:07:56,729 --> 00:07:58,729
After all, I know all of your secrets

103
00:07:58,729 --> 00:08:01,729
Try to tear me down all you want

104
00:08:01,729 --> 00:08:05,729
But if Mika, Gurin or Shinoa and the others need my help

105
00:08:05,729 --> 00:08:08,729
I'll do whatever it takes to keep them safe

106
00:08:08,729 --> 00:08:12,729
Oh yeah? You're stronger than the last time we talked

107
00:08:12,729 --> 00:08:17,729
To be honest, this new devil-may-care attitude of yours is sort of annoying

108
00:08:17,729 --> 00:08:19,729
What are you gonna do about it?

109
00:08:19,729 --> 00:08:21,729
I'm gonna kill you

110
00:08:21,729 --> 00:08:29,729
What the hell are you doing?

111
00:08:29,729 --> 00:08:33,729
I didn't come here because I want to hurt you

112
00:08:33,729 --> 00:08:35,729
Then what do you want?

113
00:08:35,729 --> 00:08:37,729
I need you, Ashuromaru

114
00:08:37,729 --> 00:08:38,729
Your strength

115
00:08:38,729 --> 00:08:40,729
Will you help me save Mika?

116
00:08:40,729 --> 00:08:44,729
I suppose I could, but what's in it for me if I do?

117
00:08:44,729 --> 00:08:47,729
If you help me, then I'll be your friend

118
00:08:47,729 --> 00:08:50,729
It's tough being alone

119
00:08:50,729 --> 00:08:53,729
And difficult to feel like you're unwanted or that you've been abandoned

120
00:08:53,729 --> 00:08:55,729
I know what that's like

121
00:08:55,729 --> 00:08:58,729
And you think being my friend will change all of that?

122
00:08:58,729 --> 00:09:00,729
Yeah

123
00:09:08,729 --> 00:09:10,729
He's awake!

124
00:09:10,729 --> 00:09:12,729
Hey

125
00:09:12,729 --> 00:09:15,729
I hope I didn't cause you guys to worry or anything

126
00:09:15,729 --> 00:09:16,729
You're back

127
00:09:16,729 --> 00:09:18,729
I mean, it's really you, right?

128
00:09:18,729 --> 00:09:21,729
Jeez, you look like you were gonna die on us there for a minute

129
00:09:21,729 --> 00:09:24,729
Oh, sorry, I didn't know what was going on with my body

130
00:09:24,729 --> 00:09:27,729
So, were you actually successful?

131
00:09:27,729 --> 00:09:32,729
And I guess it was worth it

132
00:09:32,729 --> 00:09:34,729
Am I the only one who's exhausted from all this?

133
00:09:34,729 --> 00:09:37,729
Let's just wait to do Komizuki's training later

134
00:09:37,729 --> 00:09:39,729
Huh? No way, we're doing it right now

135
00:09:39,729 --> 00:09:41,729
It's getting late and honestly, I'm kinda hungry

136
00:09:41,729 --> 00:09:43,729
No one cares if you're hungry

137
00:09:43,729 --> 00:09:45,729
Well, it took you long enough

138
00:09:45,729 --> 00:09:47,729
So, how was it? Are you okay?

139
00:09:47,729 --> 00:09:50,729
I guess you were able to fight off the psychological attacks

140
00:09:50,729 --> 00:09:53,729
Yeah, but I knew I wasn't alone

141
00:09:53,729 --> 00:09:55,729
Not now that I have you guys

142
00:09:55,729 --> 00:09:56,729
Huh?

143
00:09:56,729 --> 00:09:58,729
Never mind

144
00:09:58,729 --> 00:09:59,729
It's nothing

145
00:10:01,729 --> 00:10:02,729
Well, to put it simply

146
00:10:02,729 --> 00:10:05,729
The humans are being blinded by their desire to defeat us

147
00:10:05,729 --> 00:10:09,729
And are partaking in forbidden experimentation they don't fully understand

148
00:10:09,729 --> 00:10:11,729
It's quite unsettling

149
00:10:11,729 --> 00:10:16,729
If you'll just watch this recording, you'll understand exactly what I mean

150
00:10:16,729 --> 00:10:41,729
What was that thing?

151
00:10:41,729 --> 00:10:44,729
This could be disastrous for us

152
00:10:44,729 --> 00:10:49,729
There, you see? The humans have finally succeeded

153
00:10:49,729 --> 00:10:52,729
They have managed to weaponize the Seraph of the End

154
00:10:52,729 --> 00:10:55,729
I don't have to tell you what a serious problem this is

155
00:10:55,729 --> 00:11:02,729
But Queen Cruel put an end to the humans' experiments when she exterminated the Hyakuya sect

156
00:11:02,729 --> 00:11:04,729
That's right

157
00:11:04,729 --> 00:11:06,729
This program was dismantled eight years ago

158
00:11:06,729 --> 00:11:12,729
I killed the researchers and every child carrying even a trace of the Seraph of the End with my own hands

159
00:11:12,729 --> 00:11:16,729
Oh-ho! You're sure you killed all the test subjects?

160
00:11:16,729 --> 00:11:18,729
That's what I said, isn't it?

161
00:11:18,729 --> 00:11:22,729
But if that's true, then how has the research come so far?

162
00:11:22,729 --> 00:11:29,729
There were no organizations anywhere close to this sort of success other than the Hyakuya sect

163
00:11:29,729 --> 00:11:36,729
Cool, I'm afraid that if your leadership failed, this could end up a major liability for the other

164
00:11:36,729 --> 00:11:39,729
Hold your tongue less, Carr, or I'll have it ripped out and hung on my wall!

165
00:11:39,729 --> 00:11:43,729
Oh, have I touched a nerve? Perhaps this is too much for you

166
00:11:43,729 --> 00:11:46,729
Maybe it's time I stepped in as the new ruler of Japan

167
00:11:46,729 --> 00:11:48,729
Don't push me, little brat

168
00:11:48,729 --> 00:11:52,729
You're only 200 years older than me, Cruel

169
00:11:52,729 --> 00:11:54,729
Besides, we both know that I'm stronger

170
00:11:54,729 --> 00:11:55,729
Oh, come now!

171
00:11:55,729 --> 00:11:56,729
Please don't argue!

172
00:11:56,729 --> 00:11:58,729
Let's remember why we're here

173
00:11:58,729 --> 00:12:02,729
How do we respond to the humans' successful weaponization?

174
00:12:02,729 --> 00:12:05,729
What would you ask us to do, Queen Cruel?

175
00:12:05,729 --> 00:12:07,729
This doesn't change our basic strategy

176
00:12:07,729 --> 00:12:11,729
We'll send our strongest units in to destroy the demon army!

177
00:12:11,729 --> 00:12:13,729
Looking forward to your success

178
00:12:17,729 --> 00:12:19,729
By the way, Ferret Bathory

179
00:12:19,729 --> 00:12:22,729
Who is the young boy standing behind you?

180
00:12:22,729 --> 00:12:35,729
What the hell do you think you're doing?!

181
00:12:37,729 --> 00:12:39,729
How dare you spring that video on me!

182
00:12:39,729 --> 00:12:41,729
And bringing Mikayla along as well!

183
00:12:41,729 --> 00:12:43,729
Conspire against me and I'll end you!

184
00:12:43,729 --> 00:12:45,729
So scary!

185
00:12:45,729 --> 00:12:47,729
But you forget that you can't kill me

186
00:12:47,729 --> 00:12:49,729
After all, if I died

187
00:12:49,729 --> 00:12:51,729
Think about what might happen

188
00:12:51,729 --> 00:12:53,729
All the information I've collected on you

189
00:12:53,729 --> 00:12:55,729
Could leak to the Progenitor Council

190
00:12:57,729 --> 00:13:00,729
Besides, if they found out I let you escape

191
00:13:00,729 --> 00:13:02,729
I'd be punished too

192
00:13:03,729 --> 00:13:06,729
Dear, with all these shared secrets

193
00:13:06,729 --> 00:13:08,729
It would appear that you and I have no other choice

194
00:13:08,729 --> 00:13:09,729
But to be allies

195
00:13:09,729 --> 00:13:10,729
Hooray!

196
00:13:15,729 --> 00:13:16,729
You might even say

197
00:13:16,729 --> 00:13:17,729
We belong together

198
00:13:20,729 --> 00:13:21,729
Ah, who am I kidding?

199
00:13:25,729 --> 00:13:27,729
What a fun game this is turning out to be!

200
00:13:34,729 --> 00:13:35,729
Cruel

201
00:13:38,729 --> 00:13:47,729
Kameizuki! You have to bite it!

202
00:13:47,729 --> 00:14:02,729
Talk to me, Shinoa!

203
00:14:02,729 --> 00:14:04,729
Was I just messed up?!

204
00:14:04,729 --> 00:14:06,729
No, we might be in for a little trouble with him

205
00:14:06,729 --> 00:14:12,349
trouble with him. I think the demon might be trying to take over his body. What? What are we

206
00:14:12,349 --> 00:14:17,789
supposed to do if it does? You! I need you to be ready to attack just in case.

207
00:14:29,949 --> 00:14:36,709
Die! He's so desperate. I'll make you yield to me, Kisekiyo.

208
00:14:37,289 --> 00:14:39,989
If that's the goal, you're gonna have to try harder.

209
00:14:50,029 --> 00:14:53,029
Poor little weakling. Your body is all mine.

210
00:14:55,929 --> 00:14:57,449
Now to break you.

211
00:15:06,729 --> 00:15:14,369
Big brother.

212
00:15:15,989 --> 00:15:16,909
Don't worry.

213
00:15:16,909 --> 00:15:29,329
So, how's Mirai doing?

214
00:15:29,709 --> 00:15:32,029
Not good. I think she's getting worse.

215
00:15:33,029 --> 00:15:37,729
Look, we've got a problem. Food's running out. We won't last three days with what we've got.

216
00:15:38,209 --> 00:15:39,369
What are we gonna do?

217
00:15:40,029 --> 00:15:42,429
Leave. Tomorrow morning at the crack of dawn.

218
00:15:43,389 --> 00:15:46,789
Can't we wait longer? I'll have to figure out how to move Mirai.

219
00:15:46,789 --> 00:15:49,469
You have to leave her behind. She'd just slow us down.

220
00:15:50,009 --> 00:15:51,189
Are you out of your mind?

221
00:15:52,129 --> 00:15:58,629
Hey, calm down. We have to be logical. Your sister is way beyond our help. It sucks, but

222
00:15:58,629 --> 00:16:03,309
we've got to look out for the little ones who've survived, not to mention our own lives. It's

223
00:16:03,309 --> 00:16:11,189
a crappy world, Kimizuki. And we can't save everyone. You take care of her. It's what's best for all of us.

224
00:16:11,189 --> 00:16:14,369
You monster. How could you?

225
00:16:14,389 --> 00:16:19,989
Mirai's the one who came up with the idea. She said she doesn't want to get in your way,

226
00:16:20,509 --> 00:16:24,429
but she can't take her own life because she's too weak. Come on.

227
00:16:28,289 --> 00:16:31,749
If you can't man up and follow through with this, then I'll do it myself.

228
00:16:36,069 --> 00:16:36,869
Hold on!

229
00:16:39,509 --> 00:16:40,689
Wait! Kimizuki!

230
00:16:41,189 --> 00:16:51,049
Open the door! Let us in!

231
00:16:51,789 --> 00:16:54,269
Crap! This way! We'll climb over the balcony!

232
00:16:59,069 --> 00:17:00,549
Why do you have a knife?

233
00:17:01,469 --> 00:17:02,029
Dammit!

234
00:17:02,909 --> 00:17:08,869
Hey, big brother. I don't want to see you wasting away just because I'm too sick to get out of bed.

235
00:17:08,869 --> 00:17:10,389
Shut up, Mirai.

236
00:17:12,949 --> 00:17:15,269
Brother, please kill me.

237
00:17:16,789 --> 00:17:21,829
Do it now and it'll all be over before you know it. You'll be free to live your life however you want.

238
00:17:21,889 --> 00:17:25,569
Shut up! Just shut up! How can you say things like that?

239
00:17:25,569 --> 00:17:29,969
I can hear your thoughts. Just now you were wondering what it'd be like to be rid of me.

240
00:17:31,489 --> 00:17:37,829
I'm sick of taking care of her. She's holding me back. I'm just a kid too. I shouldn't have to do this.

241
00:17:37,829 --> 00:17:40,709
If I could just kill my sister right here.

242
00:17:41,129 --> 00:17:42,029
I didn't.

243
00:17:42,109 --> 00:17:45,749
Wouldn't it be easier if I ran away from this burden and never left back?

244
00:17:46,069 --> 00:17:47,929
That's what you just thought, big brother.

245
00:17:48,129 --> 00:17:48,809
Shut up!

246
00:17:48,809 --> 00:17:53,849
I'm not wrong, Shiho Kamizuki. Follow your instincts and free yourself.

247
00:17:58,089 --> 00:18:01,309
Thank you, big brother, for finally putting me out of my misery.

248
00:18:02,969 --> 00:18:04,509
I'm so sorry, Mirai.

249
00:18:04,509 --> 00:18:10,209
You don't need to apologize. This was all my idea, remember? It's what I wanted.

250
00:18:11,529 --> 00:18:13,809
Before I do this, can I ask you something?

251
00:18:14,569 --> 00:18:18,149
I recently met this really stupid guy who I absolutely hate.

252
00:18:18,949 --> 00:18:23,469
Now I can't seem to get away from him even though he might be the most annoying person on the planet.

253
00:18:25,209 --> 00:18:29,049
Anyway, he says he'll risk his life to protect the people he cares about.

